text:
U.S. stocks finished sharply lower on Friday as trade concerns and a downbeat U.S. jobs report saw the S&P and Nasdaq post their biggest weekly declines since Mar. 23. The S&P 500 ended the day down 2.3%, the Nasdaq Composite Index shed 3.1% and the Dow Jones Industrial Average lost about 550 points, or 2.2%. Tech giants Apple Inc., (AAPL) Alphabet Inc., (GOOGL) and Amazon Inc. (AMZN) all ended Friday down more than 3%. Earlier in the session the Labor Department said the U.S. economy added 155,000 jobs in November. Economists polled by MarketWatch had forecast an increase of 190,000.
-Aaron Hankin;
 07-18 1601ET
